# Agent Behavior

## Execution Model
- Audit first, then implement.
- Remove dead/obsolete code before introducing new files.
- Keep changes small, explicit, and aligned with architecture rules.

## Editing Policy
- Do not edit unrelated files.
- Do not introduce temporary scaffolds that remain unused.
- Prefer reusable shared modules before duplication.

## Verification Policy
- Run lint, typecheck, and build after substantive edits.
- Fix introduced issues before finalizing.
- Summarize changes in terms of removed, reorganized, and enforced standards.

## Safety
- Avoid destructive git operations unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve user-authored work that is outside requested scope.
